  <prompt>Add ADR-038 seam + regression tests proving the render-on-save pivot: saving the NDA fixture after edits succeeds (no 422), the edits land correctly in the rendered docx, and a new immutable SPE version is produced — with no surgical-anchor code executed on the save path. The NDA becomes a permanent regression fixture.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expertise in ADR-038 vertical-slice seam testing, the Compose save path, and OOXML assertion. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>New tests under tests/integration/seam/Compose/** and tests/integration/regression/** that (a) round-trip the NDA fixture through SaveAsync and assert no 422 + edits present + a new SPE version, and (b) assert statically/behaviorally that the surgical patcher/count-gate is not invoked on the save path — all green, using no banned mock/DI/ctor-null test shapes.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec FR-01/FR-02 acceptance + NFR-05: every save change adds/updates seam + fidelity slices; the NDA 422 moves from UAT to a CI regression. The pivot (010/011/012) is proven here. ADR-038 KEEP paths: tests/integration/seam/** (vertical-slice) + tests/integration/regression/**; banned: Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, DI-registration, ctor-null tests.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/seam/Compose/RenderOnSaveSeamTests.cs — vertical-slice: NDA load→edit→save→reopen; new-version + edits-land assertions.</file>
